Moments before sending Dinkum to the SOURCES.GAMES moderator I stupidly put
a bug on Dinkum which prevents compilation under DOS/TURBO-C Ver. 2 . The
correction shown below does not effect the game when compiled under Unix. 
Please modify the file "dink_sym.h" as follows:

       .....
/* True only if compiled under UNIX */
#ifndef __TURBOC__
#define void	int
#endif
#define void	int     <-----------------   DELETE this line!
       .....

With this correction Dinkum has been tested to compile under DOS/TURBO-C
Ver. 2 (I don't know about Ver. 1).  I've received a report that it will
not compile under Microsoft C.  If someone can get it to compile under
Microsoft C then please let me know how you did it (I don't have access
to that compiler).  I've received many reports of successful compilation
under different flavors of Unix, so I think Dinkum is OK in the Unix
environment.  I've put a successful Turbo-C Version 2 Makefile as a trailer
to this posting.

                            Gary


Turbo-C Version 2 Makefile:
------------------------------------------------------------------------
CFLAGS =  -c -w -mh -O
HEAD = dink_sym.h dink_glb.h
dinkum.exe: dinkum.obj describe.obj longdsc.obj objlook.obj actor.obj \
monster.obj opener.obj gleeper.obj parse.obj taker.obj
   tlink /x c:\tc\lib\c0h dinkum describe longdsc objlook actor monster \
opener gleeper parse taker, dinkum, dinkum, c:\tc\lib\ch

dinkum.obj: dinkum.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) dinkum.c
describe.obj: describe.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) describe.c
longdsc.obj: longdsc.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) longdsc.c
objlook.obj: objlook.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) objlook.c
parse.obj: parse.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) parse.c
actor.obj: actor.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) actor.c
monster.obj: monster.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) monster.c
opener.obj: opener.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) opener.c
gleeper.obj: gleeper.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) gleeper.c
taker.obj: taker.c $(HEAD)
	tcc $(CFLAGS) taker.c




